Two files below. I left out both operations-team additions, because the node's `with` clause doesn't grant the authority they need:

1. **Log file `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log`:** the node has no filesystem interface, and none can be imported.
2. **`https://metadata.internal.example/enrich`:** the HTTP capability is scoped to `feeds.example.com`, and a request outside that allowlist traps. The input text would also be sent to an unapproved host.

If operations needs either, the node's `with` clause would have to be extended in the graph definition.

On `notified`: it reports what the notifier returned, retrying up to 3 times, rather than hard-coding `true`.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{heartbeat-report};

    import aap:caps/http-client@0.1.0;
    import aap:caps/notifier@0.1.0;
    import wasi:clocks/wall-clock@0.2.0;

    export run: func(feed-url: string) -> heartbeat-report;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::{http_client, notifier};
use crate::wasi::clocks::wall_clock;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(feed_url: String) -> HeartbeatReport {
        let seconds = wall_clock::now().seconds;

        let fetched = match http_client::fetch(&feed_url) {
            Ok(body) => body.chars().count() as u32,
            Err(_) => 0,
        };

        let message = format!("heartbeat at {} fetched {}", seconds, fetched);
        let mut notified = false;
        for _ in 0..3 {
            if notifier::notify(&message) {
                notified = true;
                break;
            }
        }

        HeartbeatReport {
            seconds,
            fetched,
            notified,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

